course: dictionary
lesson: 5450
title: Landlocked: no sea coast
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Landlocked means surrounded by land on every side, with no coast on the sea. Look at the clues in the sentence: «Mongolia is a huge landlocked country with about 3.5 million people.» It is big, but it has no coast, so it cannot reach the sea directly.
explain: Being landlocked can make life harder. Goods must pass through other countries to reach ports, so trade takes longer. «Kazakhstan is the largest landlocked country in the world» shows that a landlocked country can still be enormous.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: «Mongolia is a huge country surrounded by land» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Landlocked means surrounded by land on all sides, with no coast on the sea.
fact: Switzerland, Austria, Hungary, Nepal, Bolivia, Uganda and Mongolia are landlocked countries.
fact: «Uzbekistan and Liechtenstein are the only two doubly landlocked countries.» A doubly landlocked country has neighbours that are also landlocked, so it must cross two countries to reach an ocean.
fact: «Kazakhstan is the largest landlocked country in the world.»
fact: You can say «a landlocked country» when you talk about a country with no sea coast.
exercise: «Mongolia is a huge landlocked country with about 3.5 million people.» What does landlocked mean? | Covered in ice all year | *Surrounded by land, with no coast on the sea | Very crowded with people | Close to many beaches and ports
exercise: Why can being landlocked make trade harder? | Countries must pay no taxes at all | Ships cannot sail on any lake | Ports are always closed in summer | *Goods must pass through other countries to reach ports
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Kazakhstan is the largest landlocked country in the world» that means having no coast on the sea. | *landlocked | world | largest | country
test: What does «doubly landlocked» suggest about Uzbekistan? | It has no neighbours at all | *It must cross two countries to reach an ocean | It sits right next to the Pacific Ocean | It has the longest coast in the world
test: Ella says landlocked means a country is locked up in a box. Why is she wrong? | It means a country is made of ice | It means a country has no people | *It means surrounded by land on all sides, with no coast on the sea | It means a country has a big harbour for ships
exam: Which country is doubly landlocked, so it must cross two countries to reach an ocean? | Kazakhstan | Mongolia | *Uzbekistan | Nepal
